cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use pygeovision in your research or operational work, please cite it
  using the metadata below. Citing the software helps the authors demonstrate
  research impact and continue development.

type: software
title: "pygeovision: A Unified Open-Source Python Platform for Satellite Earth Observation AI"
version: 2.0.9
date-released: "2026-07-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/eocoreint/pygeovision"
url: "https://pygeovision.readthedocs.io"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX   # updated automatically by Zenodo on each release

abstract: >
  pygeovision is a unified open-source Python library for satellite Earth
  observation analysis and geospatial AI inference. Built on pygeofetch — a
  companion library abstracting satellite data access across 22+ providers —
  pygeovision covers the complete EO workflow: SAR and optical preprocessing,
  spectral index computation, cloud masking, change detection, flood mapping,
  SAR interferometry (InSAR), and inference via foundation models including
  Prithvi-EO-2.0 and DINOv3. A natural-language query interface (GeoAgent)
  allows users to describe an analysis in plain English. pygeovision is designed
  to make operational EO analysis accessible to researchers and government
  analysts in Africa and the Global South.

authors:
  - family-names: "Appiah Kubi"
    given-names: "Samuel"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # replace with real ORCID
    affiliation: "EOCoreINT, Accra, Ghana"
    email: "appiahkubis14@gmail.com"

keywords:
  - earth observation
  - remote sensing
  - synthetic aperture radar
  - SAR
  - Sentinel-1
  - Sentinel-2
  - deep learning
  - geospatial AI
  - InSAR
  - flood mapping
  - deforestation
  - Africa
  - Global South

